  "help.body": "Crewboard — plans and worker runs\n\nPlans\n  {prog} init [--goal \"goal\"]\n  {prog} plan list | new <id> --goal \"…\" | split <id> --from <plan> --goal \"…\" --tasks a,b,c\n               | use <id> | archive <id> | unarchive <id> | rename <id> --goal \"…\"\n  {prog} chat unbind <plan>\n                                           multiple plans in a repository; commands use the current one, --plan <id> another\n  {prog} status [--json] [--plan id]\n  {prog} wait [--for decision|finished|check|any] [--tasks a,b] [--plan id] [--interval 15s] [--timeout 30m] [--json]\n                                           orchestrator: run in background; exit 0 = a decision, a finished worker or a check step, 2 = timeout, 1 = error\n                                           waits for the next change; with --tasks, if every listed task is already there\n                                           (finished, checked, decided or closed), exit 0 at once and print them marked «already»;\n                                           default --timeout 30m\n  {prog} task add <id> --title \"…\" [--kind implement|review|research|decision|root] [--lane \"…\"]\n                [--deps a,b] [--worker <profile>|auto] [--contract <file>] [--class code|design|review|research] [--backlog]\n  {prog} task set <id> [--title] [--lane] [--deps a,b] [--worker <profile>|auto] [--contract] [--status backlog|ready]\n                [--kind implement|review|research|decision|root]   --kind: only an open task (not accepted or superseded)\n                                           --worker: the preset decides — agents, do not pass it; a worker outside the preset\n                                           is refused (exit 2) unless a person runs it in a terminal; auto clears the choice\n  {prog} verify <id>                         orchestrator: take finished work for checking (agents allowed)\n  {prog} verify <id> --done --note \"…\"      checked: gates, stand, fixes — then it waits for the person\n  {prog} start <id>                          orchestrator: take a root task (your own work) in work\n  {prog} verify <id> --done --note \"…\" [--report <file>]\n                                           root task: done, goes to review; decision: prepared (options, recommendation),\n                                           only then it reaches the person; the report starts with a Result: line\n  {prog} verify <id> --return \"findings\"    back to the worker with the findings (a new run in the same worktree)\n  {prog} verify --setting on|off|default [--scope plan|repo]\n                                           orchestrator checks finished work; default: on while the plan has a chat\n  {prog} accept <id>                         human only (interactive terminal); accepted work still has to be merged —\n                                           dependents wait for the merge, the commands are printed after acceptance\n  {prog} reject <id> --reason \"…\"            human only: send back with a reason\n  {prog} supersede <id> --by <id>            human only: an alternative lost the comparison\n  {prog} drop <id> --reason \"…\"              human only: close a task that is no longer needed; it never becomes ready again\n\nRuns\n  {prog} run <id> -a <profile> [--scope s] [--contract f] [--skip-preflight]\n                                           dsh agents: -a dsh or -a dsh/<model> (for example dsh/deepseek-flash)\n  {prog} run <id>                            without -a — the task's assigned worker; with none, the preset order for the class\n                                           -a is a person's choice: agents, do not pass it — outside the preset it is refused\n                                           (exit 2); if another worker is needed, ask the person. -a auto clears the choice\n  {prog} run <id> --allow-unmerged            human only: start although a dependency is accepted but not merged —\n                                           the copy then lacks that work\n  {prog} events <id>\n  {prog} trace <id> [--json]                trace: turns, model, tools, directions\n  {prog} steer <id> (--message \"…\" | --file f) [--mode auto|queue|interrupt] [--relaunch] [--skip-preflight]\n  {prog} stop <id>\n  {prog} continue <id>                       a run that ended without a report and left uncommitted work:\n                                           a new run in the same worktree, told to finish and report\n  {prog} attention [--all] [--json] [--alarms]\n                                           what waits on a person — the screen's «Needs you»: reviews, decisions,\n                                           accepted work not merged, failed or stalled runs, other plans; --alarms: run alarms only\n  {prog} cost [--json]                       per worker: cash (money charged) and estimate (API rates for\n                                           subscription runs), never summed; JSON totals: cashUsd, apiEquivalentUsd\n\nWorkers\n  {prog} workers                             registry and worker order by task class\n  {prog} workers add <id> --kind … --model … --label … | rm <id>\n  {prog} workers disable <id> --reason \"…\" | enable <id> | route <class> <id,id,…>\n\nEnvironment\n  {prog} preflight [-a <profile>] [--probe] [--json]\n  {prog} worktree prepare <id> [--scope s]\n  {prog} worktree list\n  {prog} worktree gc [--yes]                 without --yes only shows reasons and sizes, removes nothing;\n                                           --yes removes and lists what it removed, or why everything stays\n  {prog} worktree gc --force <id>            --force is human only: remove a copy with changes\n",
